{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551261-ideas-for-derangement-dav20","id":1551261,"title":"Ideas for Derangement (DAv20)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-24T09:14:03-07:00","id":1551261,"title":"Ideas for Derangement (DAv20)","content":"Hi there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I need help coming up with a derangement for my character, and figured that this forum is filled with interesting people who have creative ideas.<br /> <br /> Long story very short:<br /> - My character had committed diablerie on another vampire, who happened to be the long-lost lover of a powerful Elder.<br /> - This Elder, once it got hold of me, wanted to dismantle my soul so that it could find their old lover and bring it to the surface. With advanced sorceries and disciplines, this process began. They never found anything, and so just kept digging through.<br /> - I was rescued, had lost most of my willpower, and hung on purely because of my character's ironclad faith in that everything happens for a reason - there was no point giving in to the darkness, since this was all meant to be and I would come out stronger for it.<br /> <br /> Basically, they were chilling on St. Peter's porch for a while as their soul was being picked apart by an insane necromancer. Traumatic stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for ways to make an interesting derangement out of this. My GM and I work together to make this fun to play with, so they're not excluded from final decisions. We're more interested in making this a narrative derangement, rather than giving it a bunch of mechanical effects.<br /> <br /> Some of the ideas I've had so far:<br /> - Addiction to life. Needing to be around people, gorging on blood, feeling the warmth of the living. Escape from the cold, dark void.<br /> - Seeking out the feeling of emptiness, either to try to master it or as a form of self harm (possibly both).<br /> - Seeking to become like the person I diablerized, a feeling of &quot;the Elder was right to try to awaken them&quot;.<br /> - Something about trusting fate to an unhealthy degree.<br /> <br /> Further ideas and suggestions would be lovely. Thanks in advance for taking the time to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}